      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "Japanese is awkward. \nどうして来ないのですか。\nWhy don't you come?\nどうして来るのですか。招待していなのに。\nWhy do you come?",
      "html": "Japanese is awkward. <br/>どうして来ないのですか。<br/>Why don't you come?<br/>どうして来るのですか。招待していなのに。<br/>Why do you come?",
      "credits_raw": "Miki",
      "content_sha256": "95b34be9d2febe85e63c12151f8e7fee92b10bda86e3f2b2c46420bc5350bed5",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 4,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "Do you know「来る」カ行変格活用?",
      "html": "Do you know「来る」カ行変格活用?",
      "credits_raw": "Miki",
      "content_sha256": "f93222d86a93f71ceab91dfb5172c5e8390679f92d3eb6c53dae78e84caf7dfc",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 5,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "→Kuru's 'ka' line conjugation? ;-)\n-ve くる→こない",
      "html": "→Kuru's 'ka' line conjugation? ;-)<br/>-ve くる→こない",
      "credits_raw": "Amatuka",
      "content_sha256": "89a2c39d87f35b342acf6126390475ffa9914958844539e5432c1c5abbaf6b96",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 6,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "I don't know if it help you lean 来る conjugation. It is also said to be カ行の三段 in a dictionary but I leant as カ行変格活用 at school as a child.\n「こ・き・くる・くる・くれ・こい」\n来ない・来ます・来る。・来るとき・来れば・来い！",
      "html": "I don't know if it help you lean 来る conjugation. It is also said to be カ行の三段 in a dictionary but I leant as カ行変格活用 at school as a child.<br/>「こ・き・くる・くる・くれ・こい」<br/>来ない・来ます・来る。・来るとき・来れば・来い！",
      "credits_raw": "Miki",
      "content_sha256": "632dfc9105f2c23c60300e8f422f664d036a50325b1ecab95fdc8009d37057f8",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 7,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "どうして来るのですか。招待していなのに。\nWhy do you come?\n\nThe above is rather ambiguous. The English translation should be \"Why do you want to come,even when not invited.\" \n\nBesides, the expression is pretty rude. Consider: どうしてお出でになりたいのですか、ご招待申しあげてもいませんのに.",
      "html": "どうして来るのですか。招待していなのに。<br/>Why do you come?<br/><br/>The above is rather ambiguous. The English translation should be \"Why do you want to come,even when not invited.\" <br/><br/>Besides, the expression is pretty rude. Consider: どうしてお出でになりたいのですか、ご招待申しあげてもいませんのに.",
      "credits_raw": "bamboo4",
      "content_sha256": "259d20a68bd287ee2f0106d57632de10ef937d814c053446e93f6eade5c693c3",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 8,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "bamboo\n\nI have never said \"why do you want to come, even when not invited\" in my entire life. (native English speaker)\n\nA natural translation would be \"Why are you coming? I didn`t invite you.\" \n\nEnglish is a little more direct than Japanese. translating a phrase word for word never sounds natural.",
      "html": "bamboo<br/><br/>I have never said \"why do you want to come, even when not invited\" in my entire life. (native English speaker)<br/><br/>A natural translation would be \"Why are you coming? I didn`t invite you.\" <br/><br/>English is a little more direct than Japanese. translating a phrase word for word never sounds natural.",
      "credits_raw": "tigert",
      "content_sha256": "1f79ed1d9c6e63b2fee7e6bd4ce2fb0d1a2a768cd61ce89c0f3c91070ec40215",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    }
